  <prompt>Remove ComposeShadowPatchEngine and the ComposeBaselineParaIdStamper count-gate from the SaveAsync path, retaining the surgical engine ONLY for the transitional clean-apply path explicitly permitted by the ADR-049 amendment. Prove by static reachability that no normal save invokes the surgical patcher or the count-gate.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Deep expertise in the Compose save path, reachability analysis, and the ADR-049 Path-B amendment. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>No code path reachable from ComposeService.SaveAsync (for a normal save) invokes ComposeShadowPatchEngine or the ComposeBaselineParaIdStamper count-gate; both types remain in the codebase for the transitional clean-apply path; docxBridge.ts is untouched; the BFF builds green and the NDA-class w14:paraId/count mismatch no longer refuses a save.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>spec FR-02: the count-gate (ComposeBaselineParaIdStamper.cs:113) and ComposeShadowPatchEngine are removed from the save path once render-on-save (010/011) is in place. The surgical engine is retained only for a transitional clean-apply path the amendment permits — it is NOT deleted. This task finalizes the retirement wiring and proves reachability.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeService.cs — remove surgical-patch + count-gate invocations from the save path.</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeBaselineParaIdStamper.cs:113 — the count-gate; ensure it is not reached from a normal SaveAsync (retain the type).</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeShadowPatchEngine.cs — retained ONLY for transitional clean-apply per the amendment; do not delete.</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="010" status="pending">Imported cutover finalized (render-from-model is the default save path; count-gate dropped) — so the surgical patcher/stamper are unreferenced by the save path and safe to retire. (RE-SEQUENCED 2026-08-05: was deps 001,011; 010 transitively covers both + the model hub. ADR-049 amendment retains the surgical engine only for the transitional clean-apply path.)</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-049">Scope: retain ComposeShadowPatchEngine ONLY for the transitional clean-apply path named in the task-001 amendment; MUST NOT invoke it (or the count-gate) from a normal save.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: NEVER delete docxBridge.ts and do NOT delete ComposeShadowPatchEngine or ComposeBaselineParaIdStamper types — retire them from the save path only.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-007">Scope: keep Services/Compose byte[]-in / projection-out; no Microsoft.Graph above SpeFileStore.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-013">Scope: NO AI-internal types in Services/Compose; consume Services/Ai/PublicContracts/ seams only if needed — no fork.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-039">Scope: engine frozen — no new AI dispatch endpoint.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope (Placement Justification, root §10): modify-only of existing Services/Compose — cite .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md in the PR, verify publish size ≤60 MB (absolute + delta vs task-003 baseline), verify no new HIGH CVE, run /conflict-check before the PR.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Save-path retirement; reachability analysis; transitional clean-apply</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-049-compose-shadow-document.md</file>
